"<description>It runs 6DoF by default, world-locking both rotation and position, and the tracking mode is selectable. It also emits the glasses hot-plug and hardware-input signals: [code]key_event[/code], [code]key_state_changed[/code], [code]wearing_changed[/code], [code]brightness_changed[/code] and the rest. [code]is_tracking()[/code] reports whether a native pose was applied on the last frame, and [code]recenter()[/code] resets the forward direction. The current app [code]Camera3D[/code] supplies its transform, clipping distances, FOV fallback, cull mask, environment, attributes and other render settings to both eye cameras at runtime; the SDK&#39;s calibrated per-eye projection and IPD still take precedence.</description>\n"
"<methods>\n"
"<method name=\"is_tracking\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Whether native head tracking fed a pose on the last frame.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"recenter\">\n"
"  <return type=\"void\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
