"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Latest glasses temperature level from the hardware event funnel: [code]0[/code] NORMAL, [code]1[/code] WARM or [code]2[/code] HOT, mirroring the SDK&#39;s [code]XREALTemperatureLevel[/code], or [code]-1[/code] until the glasses first report one. It is a cached poll, with no signal, and it is the data source behind the SDK&#39;s over-temperature notification. The SDK&#39;s low-battery notification reads the Android [i]host[/i] battery rather than a glasses API, so poll that from the platform, and the SLAM state lives in [code]get_tracking_state[/code] and [code]get_tracking_reason[/code].\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"get_last_native_error_code\">\n"
"  <return type=\"int\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Latest asynchronous native error reported by the plugin, as the [code]XREALErrorCode[/code] enum value: [code]0[/code] Success, [code]1[/code] Failure and so on, or [code]-1[/code] until one arrives. It is a cached poll with no signal, mirroring the SDK&#39;s native-error notification. Pair it with [code]get_last_native_error_message()[/code] for the accompanying text.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"get_last_native_error_message\">\n"
"  <return type=\"String\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Message that accompanied the latest native error (empty string if none / not provided).\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"start_controller\">\n"
"  <return type=\"String\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Discover + create + start the NRController subsystem ([code]libnr_loader.so[/code]) and keep it alive for [code]poll_controller[/code]. Returns a one-line diagnostic (count / id / connected &amp; handheld type). The phone-as-3D-pointer source (docs/plans/input-plan.md Phase C).\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"poll_controller\">\n"
"  <return type=\"PackedFloat32Array\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  One-frame read of the live controller&#39;s raw sensors (call each frame after [code]start_controller[/code]). Returns a flat [code]PackedFloat32Array[/code], layout: [code][ok, accel.xyz(1..4), gyro.xyz(4..7), mag.xyz(7..10), touch(10), touch_xy(11..13), buttons(13)][/code]. The phone IMU ([code]accel[/code] = gravity dir via [code]-accel.normalized()[/code]) feeds the GDScript pointer fusion, since the NRController fused pose isn&#39;t available on this host.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"switch_tracking_type\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"tracking_type\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Switch the tracking mode at runtime ([code]TRACKING_6DOF[/code] / [code]TRACKING_3DOF[/code] / [code]TRACKING_0DOF[/code] / [code]TRACKING_0DOF_STAB[/code]). Returns the SDK&#39;s bool result; [code]false[/code] also when the session is not up yet.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_display_bypass_psensor\">\n"
"  <return type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"bypass\" type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Keep the glasses display on by bypassing the proximity (wear) sensor auto-off. Returns the SDK status (0 = success), or [code]-1[/code] when unavailable. The SDK no-ops until the session is live, so retry after [code]is_session_started()[/code] turns true.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_glasses_space_mode\">\n"
"  <return type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"mode\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Set the glasses spatial display mode through [code]SetGlassesSpaceMode[/code], on the One Pro X1 chip. [code]mode[/code] is the [code]NRGlassesSpaceMode[/code] enum, which is RE&#39;d and unverified, so probe 0, 1, 2 and so on on device to find follow against world-anchor. It returns the SDK status, or [code]-1[/code] when unavailable. Call it once [code]is_session_started()[/code] is true, since the SDK no-ops until NativeGlasses is ready.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"is_hmd_feature_supported\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"feature\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Whether the connected glasses support a [code]FEATURE_*[/code] capability ([code]IsHMDFeatureSupported[/code]). [code]false[/code] when unavailable. This is the device-accurate gate the SDK itself uses.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"is_camera_supported\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Whether the connected glasses have an RGB camera, through [code]IsHMDFeatureSupported(FEATURE_RGB_CAMERA)[/code]. The Air 2 Ultra reports [code]false[/code], so gate the camera on this and it is never opened there.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"get_device_resolution\">\n"
"  <return type=\"Vector2i\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"component\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  A [code]COMPONENT_*[/code] device&#39;s pixel resolution ([code]Vector2i.ZERO[/code] when unavailable).\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"get_camera_intrinsics\">\n"
"  <return type=\"PackedFloat32Array\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"component\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  A [code]COMPONENT_*[/code] camera&#39;s intrinsics as [code][fx, fy, cx, cy][/code] in pixels (empty when unavailable).\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"get_device_pose_from_head\">\n"
"  <return type=\"PackedFloat32Array\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"component\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  A [code]COMPONENT_*[/code] device&#39;s extrinsic relative to Head, as a raw Unity [code]Pose[/code] of [code][pos x,y,z, quat x,y,z,w][/code]. It is Unity left-handed, so convert it to Godot; see coordinate-systems-notes. It is empty when unavailable.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"get_camera_projection_matrix\">\n"
"  <return type=\"PackedFloat32Array\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"component\" type=\"int\" /><param index=\"1\" name=\"near\" type=\"float\" /><param index=\"2\" name=\"far\" type=\"float\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  A [code]COMPONENT_*[/code] camera&#39;s 4x4 projection matrix (16 floats, Unity column-major) for [code][near, far][/code]. Empty when unavailable.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"is_plane_detection_available\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Whether the connected glasses support plane detection. Gated by [[code]Self::is_ar_perception_available[/code]] (6DoF + no RGB camera = the Air 2 Ultra). [code]false[/code] until the session is up, so query it at toggle time, not at startup.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_plane_detection_mode\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"mode\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Enable plane detection ([code]PLANE_HORIZONTAL | PLANE_VERTICAL[/code] flags). Needs a live 6DoF session; returns the SDK bool (false when unavailable). Call after [code]is_session_started()[/code].\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"get_plane_detection_mode\">\n"
"  <return type=\"int\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Current [code]PlaneDetectionMode[/code] flags, or [code]-1[/code] when unavailable.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"poll_planes\">\n"
"  <return type=\"Dictionary\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Poll detected-plane changes since the last call. Returns [code]{ &quot;added&quot;: Array, &quot;updated&quot;: Array, &quot;removed&quot;: Array }[/code] where each added/updated entry is a [code]Dictionary { id: String, transform: Transform3D, center: Vector2, size: Vector2, alignment: int }[/code] and [code]removed[/code] is an array of id strings. Call once per frame (drives the SDK&#39;s change queue).\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"get_plane_boundary\">\n"
"  <return type=\"PackedVector2Array\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"id\" type=\"String\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Boundary polygon (plane-local points) of a detected plane, by its id string from [code]poll_planes[/code].\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"is_anchor_available\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Whether the connected glasses support spatial anchors. Gated by [[code]Self::is_ar_perception_available[/code]] (6DoF + no RGB camera = the Air 2 Ultra). [code]false[/code] until the session is up.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_anchor_enabled\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"enabled\" type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Enable/disable the anchor subsystem (call once before acquiring). Returns whether the export was present. Needs a live 6DoF session for anchors to actually track.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_anchor_mapping_dir\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"dir\" type=\"String\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Point the anchor subsystem at a writable directory for its saved-anchor map files (e.g. [code]OS.get_user_data_dir()[/code]). Call before saving/loading.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"acquire_anchor\">\n"
"  <return type=\"Dictionary\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"pose\" type=\"Transform3D\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Create a new anchor at [code]pose[/code] (a world [code]Transform3D[/code]). Returns the anchor [code]Dictionary[/code] ([code]{ id, transform, tracking_state, session_id }[/code]) or an empty dict on failure.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"poll_anchors\">\n"
"  <return type=\"Dictionary\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Poll anchor changes since the last call: [code]{ &quot;added&quot;: Array, &quot;updated&quot;: Array, &quot;removed&quot;: Array }[/code] (each added/updated entry a [code]Dictionary { id, transform, tracking_state, session_id }[/code]; [code]removed[/code] an array of id strings). Call once per frame to drive the SDK&#39;s change queue.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"save_anchor\">\n"
"  <return type=\"String\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"id\" type=\"String\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Persist an anchor (by its id from [code]poll_anchors[/code]) and return its [code]Guid[/code] key as a 32-hex string (empty on failure). Estimate quality ≥ SUFFICIENT first; enumerate saved keys yourself.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"load_anchor\">\n"
"  <return type=\"Dictionary\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"guid\" type=\"String\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Restore a saved anchor by its [code]Guid[/code] string. Returns the anchor [code]Dictionary[/code] or an empty dict.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"remove_anchor\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"id\" type=\"String\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Drop a tracked anchor by its id. Returns the SDK bool (or [code]false[/code] when unavailable).\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"remap_anchor\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"id\" type=\"String\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Re-localize an anchor into the current map. Returns the SDK bool (or [code]false[/code] when unavailable).\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"estimate_anchor_quality\">\n"
"  <return type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"id\" type=\"String\" /><param index=\"1\" name=\"pose\" type=\"Transform3D\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Estimate an anchor&#39;s save quality ([code]ANCHOR_QUALITY_*[/code]) at [code]pose[/code], or [code]-1[/code] on failure.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"is_image_tracking_available\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Whether the connected glasses support image tracking. Gated by [[code]Self::is_ar_perception_available[/code]] (6DoF + no RGB camera = the Air 2 Ultra). [code]false[/code] until the session is up.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"init_image_database\">\n"
"  <return type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"blob\" type=\"PackedByteArray\" /><param index=\"1\" name=\"image_guids\" type=\"PackedStringArray\" /><param index=\"2\" name=\"image_sizes\" type=\"PackedVector2Array\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Build a tracking database from a reference-image DB [code]blob[/code] (produced by [code]trackableImageTools[/code]) plus, per image, its baked [code]image_guids[/code] (32-hex, aligned with [code]image_sizes[/code]) and physical [code]image_sizes[/code] (metres). Returns the DB handle ([code]0[/code] on failure). Pass it to [[code]Self::set_image_database[/code]] to activate, and keep it for [[code]Self::release_image_database[/code]].\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_image_database\">\n"
"  <return type=\"void\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"handle\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Activate a database from [[code]Self::init_image_database[/code]] (pass [code]0[/code] to disable image tracking).\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"image_reference_count\">\n"
"  <return type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"handle\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Number of reference images in a database, or [code]0[/code] when unavailable.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"release_image_database\">\n"
"  <return type=\"void\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"handle\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Free a database from [[code]Self::init_image_database[/code]].\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"poll_images\">\n"
"  <return type=\"Dictionary\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Poll tracked-image changes since the last call: [code]{ &quot;added&quot;: Array, &quot;updated&quot;: Array,\n"
" &quot;removed&quot;: Array }[/code] (each added/updated entry a [code]Dictionary { id, source_image, transform,\n"
" size, tracking_state }[/code]; [code]removed[/code] an array of id strings). Call once per frame.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"is_meshing_supported\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Whether the connected glasses support depth meshing. Gated by [[code]Self::is_ar_perception_available[/code]] (6DoF + no RGB camera = the Air 2 Ultra). [code]false[/code] until the session is up.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_meshing_enabled\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"on\" type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Enable/disable depth meshing ([code]NativePerception::SetMeshingEnabled[/code]). Returns whether the call reached the SDK (perception up); poll [code]poll_mesh_blocks[/code] after enabling.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"poll_mesh_blocks\">\n"
"  <return type=\"Array\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Poll the current mesh blocks. Returns an [code]Array[/code] of [code]Dictionary { id: String, state: int,\n"
" vertices: PackedVector3Array, normals: PackedVector3Array, indices: PackedInt32Array,\n"
" labels: PackedByteArray }[/code]. [code]state == 2[/code] means the block was removed; build/update an [code]ArrayMesh[/code] per block otherwise.[br][br][code]labels[/code] is the per-vertex semantic classification, one [code]MESH_LABEL_*[/code] per vertex, so it is index-aligned with [code]vertices[/code]. It is empty when the backend classified nothing, so compare its size against [code]vertices[/code] before indexing it.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"stream_start\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"output\" type=\"String\" /><param index=\"1\" name=\"width\" type=\"int\" /><param index=\"2\" name=\"height\" type=\"int\" /><param index=\"3\" name=\"bitrate\" type=\"int\" /><param index=\"4\" name=\"fps\" type=\"int\" /><param index=\"5\" name=\"with_mic\" type=\"bool\" /><param index=\"6\" name=\"with_internal_audio\" type=\"bool\" /><param index=\"7\" name=\"with_alpha\" type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Start streaming the FPV to [code]output[/code], which is an [code]rtp://ip:port[/code] or [code]rtmp://…[/code] URL, or a local file path; the URL scheme picks local, RTMP or RTP. It returns whether the encoder started. Then feed the view&#39;s GL texture each frame through [[code]Self::stream_push_frame[/code]], from a [code]RenderingServer.call_on_render_thread[/code].\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"stream_push_frame\">\n"
"  <return type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"gl_texture_id\" type=\"int\" /><param index=\"1\" name=\"timestamp_ns\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Feed one frame to the running stream: [code]gl_texture_id[/code] from [code]RenderingServer.texture_get_native_handle[/code] on the view&#39;s texture, [code]timestamp_ns[/code] in nanoseconds. [b]Call inside a [code]RenderingServer.call_on_render_thread[/code] callback[/b] (the encoder reads the GL texture on the render thread&#39;s EGL context). Returns the encoder status ([code]0[/code] ok, [code]-1[/code] if not streaming).\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"stream_stop\">\n"
"  <return type=\"void\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Stop + tear down the FPV stream.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"is_stream_active\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Whether an FPV stream is currently active.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"is_render_texture_encoder_supported\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Whether the render-texture HW encoder behind [[code]Self::stream_start[/code]], which both FPV streaming and mp4 recording use, can run on the current renderer: [[code]Self::get_render_texture_encoder_backend[/code]] != 0. Check it BEFORE pairing, permission dialogs or other start side effects, and report the specific reason to the user; [code]stream_start[/code] keeps the hard refusal either way.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"get_render_texture_encoder_backend\">\n"
"  <return type=\"int\" />\n"
"  \n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Which backend feeds the HW encoder: [code]0[/code] = unsupported, [code]1[/code] = the GL renderer&#39;s direct texture-name push ([[code]Self::stream_push_frame[/code]]), [code]2[/code] = the Vulkan bridge (vulkan-path-plan.md stage 4), where components publish the source viewport each frame through [[code]Self::stream_publish_viewport[/code]] instead. Backend 2 is reported whenever the renderer is Vulkan with a live [code]RenderingDevice[/code], independent of the glasses kill switch (the encoder works in encoder-only mode too); the bridge itself initializes lazily at [code]stream_start[/code], and a hard init failure there turns the stream off through its error path.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"stream_publish_viewport\">\n"
"  <return type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"viewport_rid\" type=\"Rid\" /><param index=\"1\" name=\"timestamp_ns\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Vulkan backend only: publish this frame&#39;s stream source, the composed SubViewport&#39;s viewport RID, plus a nanosecond timestamp describing the frame. Call it once per frame from [code]_process[/code] while streaming or recording; the bridge copies the viewport&#39;s [code]VkImage[/code] into an encoder bundle at the end of the frame and encodes it one frame later. Returns [code]0[/code] accepted, [code]-1[/code] while the encoder is idle, [code]-2[/code] when the viewport cannot be resolved to an RGBA8-class Vulkan image (or the renderer is not the Vulkan backend).\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_stereo_mode\">\n"
"  <return type=\"void\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"mode\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Select the stereo rendering mode applied when the native session [b]bootstraps[/b], a startup selector: [code]0[/code] is Multipass, both eyes, the default shipping path, and [code]2[/code] is Multiview, single-pass-instanced. [b]Call it before the session starts[/b], for instance in an autoload [code]_ready[/code], before the XR rig enters the tree, because it is read once at [code]InitUserDefinedSettings[/code]. It is equivalent to the ProjectSetting [code]xreal/stereo_mode[/code] or to [code]adb shell setprop debug.xreal.stereo_mode &lt;n&gt;[/code]. Multiview buys nothing on this two-SubViewport rig (see docs/archive/multiview-investigation.md), so Multipass stays the recommended default.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_focus_plane\">\n"
"  <return type=\"bool\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"point\" type=\"Vector3\" /><param index=\"1\" name=\"normal\" type=\"Vector3\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Point the compositor&#39;s reprojection plane at [code]point[/code], with surface [code]normal[/code], both in [b]head-local Godot space[/b]: the head tracker&#39;s own frame, not the world. Returns whether the call reached the SDK.[br][br]Before every VSync the compositor warps the last rendered frame to the newest head pose, and it does that against a plane. Content far from that plane is what smears and doubles when the head moves. The SDK pins the plane at a fixed 1.4 m unless an app moves it, so an app whose content sits at arm&#39;s length gains from setting it to whatever the user is looking at.[br][br]This is a per-frame setting, not a mode. It holds its last value, so call it every frame, or use [code]addons/godot_xreal/features/xreal_focus_plane.tscn[/code], which drives it from a forward raycast the way the SDK&#39;s [code]FocusManager[/code] does.[br][br][code]normal[/code] points back at the viewer, so [code]Vector3(0, 0, 1)[/code], the Godot camera&#39;s backward axis, is the default for a plane square to the gaze.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_tracking_type\">\n"
"  <return type=\"void\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"mode\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Select the head-tracking mode applied when the native session [b]bootstraps[/b], a startup selector: [code]0[/code] is 6DoF, SLAM position and orientation with no drift, the recommended mode; [code]1[/code] is 3DoF, IMU orientation only with no position; and [code]2[/code] is 0DoF. [b]Call it before the session starts[/b], for instance in an autoload [code]_ready[/code], before the XR rig enters the tree, because it is read once at [code]InitUserDefinedSettings[/code]. It is equivalent to the ProjectSetting [code]xreal/tracking_type[/code] or to [code]adb shell setprop debug.xreal.tracking_type &lt;n&gt;[/code]. Use [code]get_tracking_type()[/code] for the mode actually active on the running session, and [code]switch_tracking_type()[/code] to change it at runtime, an SDK call that may be unavailable mid-session.\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
"<method name=\"set_input_source\">\n"
"  <return type=\"void\" />\n"
"  <param index=\"0\" name=\"source\" type=\"int\" />\n"
"  <description>\n"
"  Which input sources [code]InitUserDefinedSettings[/code] asks the SDK for: [code]1[/code] is Controller, the default, [code]2[/code] is Hands and [code]3[/code] is ControllerAndHands. It must be called [b]before[/b] the XR rig starts the session, because it is read once at bootstrap. It is also settable with [code]adb shell setprop debug.xreal.input_source &lt;n&gt;[/code].[br][br][b]Ask for Hands only if you actually use hand tracking.[/b] The Hands bit makes the SDK call [code]NativePerception::SetHandTrackingEnabled(true)[/code] synchronously during input start, measured at [b]about 878 ms of cold start[/b] on an X4000 with a One Pro, and hand tracking is Air 2 Ultra only, so on any other headset that is pure latency. [code]addons/godot_xreal/features/xreal_hands.tscn[/code] sets this to [code]3[/code] from its [code]_ready()[/code], so scenes that include the hands feature get it automatically and everyone else starts faster. See [code]docs/archive/codex-input-start-analysis.md[/code].\n"
"  </description>\n"
"</method>\n"
"\n"
